der 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids, more than any other pair since 1951. In 2025 that pair ran 65% of normal on the middle, and September to October fell to 53%. So far in 2026 the middle read 27% for March to April and 195% for May to June. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grid 12179 and grid 12477 at 59%.</p>"}
